<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/</link><lastBuildDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 20:40:44 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Trump threatens to ‘hit Iran hard’ as strikes resume after month-long lull</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260831-trump-threatens-to-hit-iran-hard-as-strikes-resume-after-month-long-lull</link><description>
President Donald Trump said Monday that the US would hit back against Iranian attacks on US targets in the Middle East, according to a Fox News reporter. The Iranian attacks were themselves a response to US strikes on an island in the Strait of Hormuz, the first flare-up in a month.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6620eaf0-a51e-11f1-b104-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T085336Z-115528668-RC2J9NAP5OBK-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-STRIKE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6620eaf0-a51e-11f1-b104-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T085336Z-115528668-RC2J9NAP5OBK-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-STRIKE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f6a05eba-a57a-11f1-a76a-fb7aabece8fd</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 20:36:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6620eaf0-a51e-11f1-b104-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T085336Z-115528668-RC2J9NAP5OBK-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-STRIKE.jpg">© via Reuters/Wana News Agency</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Trump vows to hit back 'hard' after first exchange of fire with Iran in weeks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/trump-vows-to-hit-back-hard-after-first-exchange-of-fire-with-iran-in-weeks</link><description>
Donald Trump threatened to hit Iran "hard" after the two foes traded fire for the first time in over a month, while Iran's president warned that more fighting with the US was not in his country's interest. After six months of war, the foes remain at an impasse, with Iran keeping the strategic Strait of Hormuz closed and the US persisting with a naval counter-blockade of Iran. FRANCE 24's Reza Sayah reports from Tehran.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/61eaaa56-8a5d-11f1-8f74-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C39X7A2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/61eaaa56-8a5d-11f1-8f74-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C39X7A2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8d277974-a56a-11f1-9374-435f773a4b38</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 18:37:10 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Raising the Altalena: Netanyahu digs up sunken 1948 arms ship in ‘pre-election stunt’</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260831-raising-altalena-netanyahu-digs-up-sunken-1948-arms-ship-irgun-pre-election-stunt</link><description>
A ship carrying arms for a right-wing militia, the Altalena was sunk 78 years ago off the coast of Tel Aviv at the orders of Israel’s founders. The discovery of its wreckage last week has given the country’s right-wing government ammunition to target the left and attempt to redirect the campaign for legislative elections in October.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0ab78be2-a2bc-11f1-a8e8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Altalena-off-Tel-Aviv-beach.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0ab78be2-a2bc-11f1-a8e8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Altalena-off-Tel-Aviv-beach.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">03fb2ff4-a54e-11f1-ba53-494925e89fd0</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 16:54:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0ab78be2-a2bc-11f1-a8e8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Altalena-off-Tel-Aviv-beach.jpg">© Wikimedia Creative Commons</source><dc:creator>Stéphanie TROUILLARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Latest flare-up between US and Iran bring conflict's lull to an end</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/latest-flare-up-between-us-and-iran-bring-conflict-s-lull-to-an-end</link><description>
Iran's foreign minister has accused Israel's Benjamin Netanyahu of tricking the United States into war with the Islamic Republic. Over six months into the conflict, there appears to be no end in sight. This after the US struck sites in Iran, prompting Tehran to respond. An April ceasefire brought an end to intense fighting, but sporadic attacks have continued over the Strait of Hormuz. Tehran's closure of the waterway during the conflict has pressured global oil markets, and in turn Donald Trump at home.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af51be10-a542-11f1-b684-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T081353Z-1164684493-RC2I9NA5KP2J-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-OMAN-HORMUZ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af51be10-a542-11f1-b684-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T081353Z-1164684493-RC2I9NA5KP2J-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-OMAN-HORMUZ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b8f0074e-a54f-11f1-a0e9-9fe11a5e0a83</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 15:33:57 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Strait of Hormuz accessibility at the centre of US-Iran war flare-up</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/strait-of-hormuz-accessibility-at-the-centre-of-us-iran-war-flare-up</link><description>
For the first time in a month, the US has launched strikes against Iran. The attack targeted the shipping island of Larak in the Strait of Hormuz. The US says it was aimed at preventing Tehran from placing sea mines in the strategic shipping lane, just days after Washington announced it had completed clearing explosives from there. Iran then reiterated its attacks, saying it had struck two US military bases in Jordan. FRANCE 24's Rochelle Ferguson-Bouyahi tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8e6966dc-a4af-11f1-a8ee-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4AZ2KD.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8e6966dc-a4af-11f1-a8ee-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4AZ2KD.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">11e4d97c-a539-11f1-b130-bb4a68c160c1</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 12:47:11 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Relentless heat worsens Gaza's ongoing struggle to access water</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/relentless-heat-worsens-gaza-s-ongoing-struggle-to-access-water</link><description>
In Gaza, securing drinking water is a relentless daily struggle. The war with Israel has destroyed critical water and sanitation infrastructure, and as temperatures soar, the extreme heat is escalating an already severe shortage into a deadly humanitarian crisis. Two and a half years of war with Israel have damaged or destroyed nearly 90% of Gaza’s water and sanitation infrastructure according to UNICEF.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/240c99ec-a529-11f1-8aad-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-9629343336a955b618609c3-22073425.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/240c99ec-a529-11f1-8aad-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-9629343336a955b618609c3-22073425.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d4d89c98-a525-11f1-8e66-9904c0de4c4a</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 10:49:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Iran, US trade fire in first exchange in a month</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260831-iran-us-trade-fire-in-first-exchange-in-a-month</link><description>
Iran attacked US military targets in the Middle East on Monday in retaliation following American strikes on an island in the Strait of Hormuz, the first exchange of fire for a month in a war that has engulfed the region.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3fa00686-a528-11f1-a2b8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/mini-29.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3fa00686-a528-11f1-a2b8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/mini-29.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9b0093ec-a528-11f1-944f-9dca7ebcfc2a</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 10:49:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Middle East war flares up after Iran responds to US attacks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east-war-flares-up-after-iran-responds-to-us-attacks</link><description>
Iran attacked US military targets in the Middle East in retaliation for the first American strikes on its territory in a month. This signs a fresh flare-up of the war that has engulfed the region. Washington said its attacks were aimed at preventing Iran from placing more sea mines in the strait and as it threatens new secondary economic sanctions. FRANCE 24's Reza Sayah is in Tehran and tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a984b044-a224-11f1-800d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26213442630871.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a984b044-a224-11f1-800d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26213442630871.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">369070de-a524-11f1-9e55-9904c0de4c4a</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 10:43:37 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US renews attack on Iran while threatening financial sanctions on Tehran allies</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-renews-attack-on-iran-while-threatening-financial-sanctions-on-tehran-allies</link><description>
Hostilities between the US and Iran resumed after a month's pause. The US said Iran was preparing to launch sea mines into the Strait of Hormuz. Iran retaliated by hitting US military bases in Jordan. Meanwhile, the US Treasury Secretary said there would be more economic sanctions on the way for banks doing business with Iran.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6620eaf0-a51e-11f1-b104-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T085336Z-115528668-RC2J9NAP5OBK-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-STRIKE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6620eaf0-a51e-11f1-b104-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T085336Z-115528668-RC2J9NAP5OBK-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-STRIKE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">be5cd37e-a51d-11f1-b08c-41b48f6f83b3</guid><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 09:40:48 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Middle East live: Iran says continuing war ‘not in our interest’ after fighting flares</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260830-middle-east-live-us-strikes-iran-for-first-time-in-a-month</link><description>
Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian said Monday that continuing the war with the United States was not in his country's interest, following a fresh military flare-up between the two countries after a month-long lull. Follow our live blog for the latest updates.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af51be10-a542-11f1-b684-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T081353Z-1164684493-RC2I9NA5KP2J-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-OMAN-HORMUZ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af51be10-a542-11f1-b684-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T081353Z-1164684493-RC2I9NA5KP2J-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-OMAN-HORMUZ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d6f7a1b4-a4c5-11f1-8a83-31d4a2f58c7c</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 23:02:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af51be10-a542-11f1-b684-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-31T081353Z-1164684493-RC2I9NA5KP2J-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-OMAN-HORMUZ.jpg">© Stringer, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>US forces strike Iranian launchers on Larak island in Strait of Hormuz</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260830-us-forces-strike-iranian-launchers-on-larak-island-in-strait-of-hormuz</link><description>
US forces struck Iranian rocket launchers on the Strait of Hormuz in the first military action in a month, a US official said Sunday. ⁠Iran's ⁠Revolutionary ​Guards ​said the attack on Larak ​island ‌killed and wounded ⁠several Iranian fighters and ​civilians, and ‌vowed to punish those ​responsible.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8e6966dc-a4af-11f1-a8ee-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4AZ2KD.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8e6966dc-a4af-11f1-a8ee-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4AZ2KD.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a1532ba2-a4af-11f1-adf9-71be596dc8a3</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 20:27:09 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8e6966dc-a4af-11f1-a8ee-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4AZ2KD.jpg">© Atta Kenare, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Netanyahu condemns violence in West Bank</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/netanyahu-condemns-violence-in-west-bank</link><description>
It was a rare condemnation from what is widely seen as the most religious and ultranationalist government in Israel’s history. Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu condemned recent attacks by Israeli settlers on Palestinians in the occupied West Bank, but described the violence as the actions of a “handful of rioters.” Tensions have surged across the territory, with activists accusing settlers of acting with impunity. Much of the recent violence has taken place in the town of Qusra. Peter O’Brien reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/27abccec-a44f-11f1-958b-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/israeli-settlers.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/27abccec-a44f-11f1-958b-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/israeli-settlers.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d4c4f894-a44b-11f1-9470-75564c8cf08f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 08:46:45 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Netanyahu condemns 'criminal acts of violence' by settlers in West Bank villages</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260829-netanyahu-condemns-criminal-acts-of-violence-by-settlers-in-west-bank-villages</link><description>
Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on Saturday condemned what he called "criminal acts of violence" perpetrated by Israeli settlers in two Palestinian villages. Earlier in August, a group of settlers blocked supplies from entering Palestinian houses on the outskirts of Qusra and attacked a Palestinian family and a foreign media crew in nearby Jalud.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c2c9d0c8-a3d4-11f1-9dfa-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6TD3PD.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c2c9d0c8-a3d4-11f1-9dfa-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6TD3PD.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7144d52c-a3d4-11f1-873f-972eeb0bc107</guid><pubDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 18:34:03 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c2c9d0c8-a3d4-11f1-9dfa-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6TD3PD.jpg">© Jaafar Ashtiyeh, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Iran war reaches 6-month mark: Conflict cost $1,100 per US taxpayer</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/iran-war-reaches-6-month-mark-conflict-cost-1-100-per-us-taxpayer</link><description>
After six months of war, Iran’s leadership has coalesced around a hard core of military generals and clerics long entrenched in the ruling theocracy. They are ready for a potentially long confrontation with the US and determined to prevent any unrest at home. It’s a far cry from US President Donald Trump’s initial hopes of toppling the Islamic Republic and his subsequent claims that “regime change” had brought more compromising officials to the fore. In an analysis, FRANCE 24's Philip Turle said the war had so far cost around 1,100 US dollars for each US taxpayer.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cce883aa-a3bc-11f1-934a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260829-170756-171246-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cce883aa-a3bc-11f1-934a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260829-170756-171246-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d1e3089e-a3bc-11f1-b84b-775873edb3f6</guid><pubDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 15:24:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Situation in Niger 'not stabilised yet' as security forces deploy around airport</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/situation-in-niger-not-stabilised-yet-as-security-forces-deploy-around-airport</link><description>
A group of soldiers in Niger rebelled against officers at a key military base and fired at sensitive locations in the capital, Niamey, in an apparent mutiny marked by gunfire and explosions, authorities said Saturday, in what was seen as a major threat to the country's struggling junta. FRANCE 24's Wassim Nasr brings you this analysis.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/78eae0be-a3b1-11f1-b639-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260829-150807-151045-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/78eae0be-a3b1-11f1-b639-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260829-150807-151045-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7dd32f14-a3b1-11f1-9a04-c7d05d6e3460</guid><pubDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 13:59:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Several killed in Israeli strikes on Gaza and West Bank</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/several-killed-in-israeli-strikes-on-gaza-and-west-bank</link><description>
Israeli strikes in Gaza have killed five people, local hospital officials said Friday. Two brothers and another relative died in a strike on the family’s home outside Khan Younis, officials at Nasser Hospital said. Two separate Israeli strikes killed one person each in Gaza City, according to health officials at Shifa hospital.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e5690b0c-a394-11f1-9545-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260829-120935-121116-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e5690b0c-a394-11f1-9545-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260829-120935-121116-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ea5586ae-a394-11f1-8b90-d1c2be3b23b1</guid><pubDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 10:34:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel army carries out rare West Bank air strike, killing 'three terrorists'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260828-israel-army-carries-out-rare-west-bank-air-strike-killing-three-terrorists</link><description>
Israel's military said it carried out an air strike in the Jenin area in the West Bank on Friday that killed a ​Palestinian it described as a Hamas militant operative as well as two of his accomplices, in a rare use of deadly Israeli air power in the occupied territory.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd7979b0-a2f5-11f1-9ae1-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-28T152358Z-1191338275-RC2R7NA7VEHT-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-JENIN-AIRSTRIKE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd7979b0-a2f5-11f1-9ae1-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-28T152358Z-1191338275-RC2R7NA7VEHT-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-JENIN-AIRSTRIKE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">45d4b240-a302-11f1-adc1-7d8ef64e4da5</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 17:14:47 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd7979b0-a2f5-11f1-9ae1-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-28T152358Z-1191338275-RC2R7NA7VEHT-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-JENIN-AIRSTRIKE.jpg">© Mohamad Torokman, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>There is no proof that this video shows a plane crash in Tel Aviv</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260828-no-proof-video-shows-plane-crash-tel-aviv</link><description>
A video showing an airplane rammed into the side of a building has been circulating widely on social media. While social media users are claiming that the video shows a plane that crashed in Tel Aviv after an Iranian attack, its origin remains unknown and its authenticity highly questionable. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7b6c19b4-a2f0-11f1-a69a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/tel-aviv-2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7b6c19b4-a2f0-11f1-a69a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/tel-aviv-2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d3e76d02-a2df-11f1-905e-4f73667cf1bc</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 15:31:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7b6c19b4-a2f0-11f1-a69a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/tel-aviv-2.jpg">© X</source><dc:creator>The FRANCE 24 Observers</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title><![CDATA[Israel's 'retrospective incrimination: First we shoot, we kill & then find a reason why it happened']]></title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/retrospective-incrimination-first-we-shoot-we-kill-and-then-we-find-a-reason-why-it-happened</link><description>
Liza Kaminov is pleased to welcome Nadav Weiman, Executive Director of Breaking the Silence. He says there is a troubling gap between how Israeli military operations in Gaza are publicly explained and what soldiers experience on the ground. Testimonies collected by Breaking the Silence suggest that this gap is not simply about individual incidents, but about the policies, assumptions and rules of engagement. The testimony surrounding the Nasser Hospital strike points to “retrospective incrimination”: rather than identifying a legitimate military target before an attack, evidence connecting those killed to Hamas may be sought afterward in order to justify the strike.
